From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add the GalaxyCore GC4023 sensor driver

Add a mainline V4L2 subdev driver for the GalaxyCore GC4023 image
sensor. The mode register sequence and gain table are adapted from the
Ingenic vendor sensor driver (sensor_gc4023_t31).

The driver uses the CCI register helpers, runtime PM, and the current
state-based subdev pad API. It exposes the full-resolution mode with
HBLANK/VBLANK, exposure, analogue gain, and mirror/flip controls where
the vendor driver provides them.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc4023.c
@@ -0,0 +1,887 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * GalaxyCore GC4023 CMOS Image Sensor Driver
+ *
+ * The register sequences and gain table are adapted from the Ingenic
+ * vendor sensor driver (sensor_gc4023_t31).
+ *
+ * WARNING: this driver has not been validated on hardware. Only the SC2336
+ * driver has been tested on a camera.
+ */
+
+#include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/i2c.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
+#include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/units.h>
+
+#include <media/v4l2-cci.h>
+#include <media/v4l2-ctrls.h>
+#include <media/v4l2-device.h>
+#include <media/v4l2-fwnode.h>
+#include <media/v4l2-mediabus.h>
+
+#define GC4023_CHIP_ID_H			0x40
+#define GC4023_CHIP_ID_L			0x23
+
+#define GC4023_REG_CHIP_ID_H			CCI_REG8(0x03f0)
+#define GC4023_REG_CHIP_ID_L			CCI_REG8(0x03f1)
+
+/* HTS is stored divided by two; VTS is a 14-bit value. */
+#define GC4023_REG_HTS				CCI_REG16(0x0342)
+#define GC4023_REG_VTS				CCI_REG16(0x0340)
+#define GC4023_REG_EXPOSURE			CCI_REG16(0x0202)
+
+#define GC4023_REG_GAIN_614			CCI_REG8(0x0614)
